    "Section 3.2.2 Recommendations": "Ongoing management of IST is recommended to focus on symptom reduction. Ivabradine, an inhibitor of the If channel, is now being used to slow the heart rate. Radiofrequency ablation targeting early activation with isoproterenol infusion may also reduce sinus rate, with reports showing success rates of 76% to 100% in nonrandomized cohorts."
